      "message": "act` is *not* imported at runtime.\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` (copied from the contract).\n- `_ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({(\"new\",\"paid\"), (\"new\",\"cancelled\"), (\"paid\",\"refunded\")})` \u2014 the v2 transition set.\n- `can_transition(old, new)` \u2014 local copy of the contract predicate: `(old, new) in _ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS`.\n- `consume(old, new)` \u2014 returns `{\"old\", \"new\", \"allowed\", \"reason\", \"contract_version\"}`; `reason` is `\"allowed\"`, `\"not-allowed\"` (both states involved are known), or `\"unknown-state\"`. It intentionally does **not** chain/closures transitions (e.g. `new\u2192refunded` is rejected, not composed as `new\u2192paid\u2192refunded`), matching the contract's single-step decision.\n\n**Local check (ran, passed)**\n- `('new','paid')`, `('new','cancelled')`, `('paid','refunded')` \u2192 `allowed: True`\n- `('new','refunded')`, `('paid','cancelled')`, `('bogus','paid')` \u2192 `allowed: False`, `reason: 'not-allowed'`\n- Confirmed no `import semkg_contract` in the source.\n\nNo other files were created or modified."
